1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Chat is the wrong shape for visual thinking.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
TRACE gives a person and an AI agent
one shared reasoning surface.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
I circle the thing I mean,
and the gesture becomes exact semantic context.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Through WebMCP, ChatGPT reads the live board
instead of guessing from pixels.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
It draws gravity, normal force, and friction
beside my block.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Then it derives the acceleration in place
and turns the equation into motion.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
These are bounded webpage operations,
not simulated clicks.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Now I reject friction with one physical mark.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
I did not write another prompt.
I changed the shared model.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Every dependent expression recomputes
from 4.06 to 4.91 metres per second squared.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The same language transfers to a domain
where certainty is dangerous.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
This straight arrow is an intentionally bad
explanation of history.

13
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
I circle it and ask what is missing.

14
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:27,000
The agent expands it into dated decisions
and interacting pressures.

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Then it places two primary-source perspectives
beneath the model.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,000
One supports alliance escalation;
the other complicates inevitability.

17
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The reasoning appears
where the question happened.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
I cross out one decision.

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,000
TRACE weakens only the paths that depend on it
and opens a possible negotiation window.

20
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
It does not pretend to predict an alternate past.
The canvas is the prompt.
